### Control Panel Wiring Rules & Noise Mitigation
1. **Galvanic Isolation:** Maintain strict separation between the 230V AC incoming line, 24V DC sensor bus, and inductive motor/valve coils.
2. **Flyback Suppression:** Fit all pneumatic solenoid coils with 1N4007 flyback diodes (or integrated MOV varistor suppressor connectors) to eliminate back-EMF spikes during de-energization.
3. **Sensor Shielding:** Sensor cables running along the conveyor aluminum extrusion must be double-shielded, with shields bonded to the control panel earth bar at one single end.
